.TH WLAN 8
.SH NAME
wlan \- wireless networks: the ones in range, joining one, the ones to know
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wlan
[
.B -d
.I dev
]
.br
.B wlan
[
.B -d
.I dev
]
.B join
[
.B -s
]
.I essid
.br
.B wlan
[
.B -d
.I dev
]
.B auto
.br
.B wlan forget
.I essid
.br
.B wlan
[
.B -d
.I dev
]
.B off
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Wlan
works on the first wireless interface (one whose
.B ifstats
has an
.B essid
line; the interfaces the boot did not bind are bound into
.B /net
first), or on
.IR dev ,
e.g.
.BR /net/ether1 .
.PP
Without a command it lists the networks the interface has heard, the
strongest first: a
.B *
for the one it is associated with, the best signal in dBm and its
channel, how many access points send it, whether it is
.B wpa
(the privacy bit) or
.BR open ,
and its name.
.PP
.B Join
leaves the network it is in and joins
.IR essid :
an open one by the interface's
.B essid
message, a protected one by
.IR wpa (8),
its passphrase from the known networks or else asked for on
.B /dev/cons
(not echoed) and put into
.IR factotum (4).
Associated, the interface gets its address by DHCP
.RI ( ipconfig (8);
an address it had is removed first).
With
.B -s
the network becomes a known one.
.PP
.B Auto
joins the strongest network in range that is known, waiting up to
.B $wlanwait
seconds (default 30) for one to be heard: at boot the radio's scan has
heard nothing yet.
.I Termrc
runs it at boot when there are known networks, unless
.B wlan=off
is in
.IR plan9.ini (8).
Within a network the interface roams between its access points by
itself (see
.IR ether (3)).
.PP
.B Forget
drops a known network and its key in factotum;
.B off
leaves the network and removes the interface's addresses.
.SH FILES
.TF $home/lib/wlan
.TP
.B $home/lib/wlan
the known networks, one per line:
.I essid
and passphrase separated by a tab (empty for an open one).
Only its owner may read it, as it holds the passphrases in clear, like
the configuration files of other systems' supplicants; they are not in
.IR secstore (1).
.PD
.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
% wlan
*  -53 dBm  ch  05  4 ap  wpa   galaxy
   -60 dBm  ch  01  1 ap  open  Cafe Free WiFi
% wlan join -s 'Cafe Free WiFi'
.EE
.SH SOURCE
.B /rc/bin/wlan
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR wpa (8),
.IR ipconfig (8),
.IR factotum (4)
.SH BUGS
It asks for the passphrase only on a console: a window system's menu
does not offer it yet.
WPA-PSK only (no 802.1X).
.PP
